   "parameters": {
    "width": 900,
    "height": 260,
    "content": "## I.LPR — LP Report Router (133–137) · thin transport ONLY, routes on the FILENAME report ID\n\nOne Gmail trigger for every LP report email → Code node extracts `_133_`…`_137_` from the attachment filename → Switch → POST raw PDF to the matching LP-MCP endpoint. ZERO parsing here. Positive IF: success=true ends clean; false (deterministic rejection) or transport error → telemetry (`onError: continueRegularOutput` — the failure path never fails the workflow). Unroutable filenames go to telemetry as `unroutable_filename`, never a silent drop.\n\n**CUTOVER (Mark):** ① reschedule 133/136/137 to YTD in LP (137 end date pinned to yesterday) — MTD pulls return blank Net/NSA/NSLI on 136/137 and understate 133's backlog ~85%; ② activate this router; ③ deactivate I.LPRA–E; ④ next morning confirm five `scorecard_ingest_log` success rows.\n\n**Endpoint state (2026-08-05):** 133/134/137 parse for real (137 built from the Aug sample; fails closed on layout drift). 135/136 fail closed with `parser_pending` — the first scheduled email archives the sample that unblocks building each parser. PDFs print whole dollars: daily figures carry the logged ±$1/row `display_rounding` allowance; monthly manual CSV pull recommended for penny reconciliation."
   }
  }
